<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n51840" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καθιππ-εύω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>ride over, overrun with horse</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ πεδία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					3.26
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hdn.
				6.2.5
			</span></i>; <i>ride upon</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἶδμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Hymn.Is.</u>
					154
				</span></i>
			; of fish, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κῦμα κ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Opp.
				<u>H.</u>
				2.515
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, of frozen rivers, <i>to be ridden over</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Mir.</u>
				846b32
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdn.
				6.7.6
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>ride down, trample under foot</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀργείων στρατόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					732
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>conquer by means of a horse</i> (i. e. the <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δούρειος ἵππος</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Tryph.
				174
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
</div>